    "body": "## Motivation\n\nSource changes invalidate the final editable-install layer, rerunning `kernels lock` and `kernels download`. The current layer filesystem cannot reuse downloads from its previous execution, even when the required kernel artifacts are unchanged.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add a BuildKit cache mount for Hugging Face kernel downloads, separated by target architecture and CUDA version, with `sharing=locked`.\n- Set `HF_HOME` only for the editable-install RUN.\n- Copy cached downloads to the existing runtime cache location before the RUN ends, because cache-mount contents are not exported in image layers.\n\nThe existing metadata resolution, retry behavior, and runtime-stage copy paths remain in place. This is the download-cache subset of a downstream build improvement; it does not add a pinned kernel lock.\n\n## Production build and deployment evidence\n\nThe downstream build improvement has successfully produced the image used by our production inference deployment. It includes both kernel metadata pinning and download caching; this PR extracts only the reusable download-cache portion.\n\nOn 2026-10-18, read-only checks confirmed the published base image manifest (HTTP 200 and a matching content digest). The deployed Dockerfile and kernel-lock input metadata matched the downstream release by SHA256. The runtime deployment snapshot showed all 14 related service pods Running and Ready with zero restarts.\n\nThese results establish a successful downstream build and deployment. The upstream extraction retains online metadata resolution, so it does not claim to fix metadata-fetch timeouts. No matched cold/warm build timing or speedup percentage is claimed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- The changed RUN's shell body passed `sh -n`.\n- A local cache-materialization fixture confirmed that `cp -a` preserves Hugging Face-style relative snapshot symlinks and that they resolve after copying.\n\nThe shared cache retains older snapshots. Copying it can grow the runtime cache as kernel revisions accumulate; architecture/CUDA-specific cache IDs avoid combining incompatible target caches.\n\n## Related work\n\n#22160 already optimized Docker dependency layering and source-copy placement. This builds on that structure by reusing kernel downloads when the source-sensitive layer must rerun.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #39127795131](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39127795131)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39127795101](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39127795101)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
